tificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 15 Jan 2026 (this version), latest version 19 Jan 2026 (cite5†v3 )]\nL9: # Title:ChartComplete: A Taxonomy-based Inclusive Chart Dataset\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Ahmad Mustapha (American University of Beirut, Lebanon), cite7†Charbel Toumieh (American University of Beirut, Lebanon), cite8†Mariette Awad (American University of Beirut, Lebanon)\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled ChartComplete: A Taxonomy-based Inclusive Chart Dataset, by Ahmad Mustapha (American University of Beirut and 5 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite9†View PDF cite10†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:With advancements in deep learning (DL) and computer vision techniques, the field of chart understanding is evolving rapidly. In particular, multimodal large language models (MLLMs) are proving to be efficient and accurate in understanding charts. To accurately measure the performance of MLLMs, the research community has developed multiple datasets to serve as benchmarks. By examining these datasets, we found that they are all limited to a small set of chart types.\nL17: To bridge this gap, we propose the ChartComplete dataset. The dataset is based on a chart taxonomy borrowed from the visualization community, and it covers thirty different chart types. The dataset is a collection of classified chart images and does not include a learning signal. We present the ChartComplete dataset as is to the community to build upon it.\nL18: Comments:  | 7 pages, 4 figures, 3 tables, 1 algorithm. Dataset and source code available at cite11†this https URL†github.com L19: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL20: ACM (Association of Computing Machinery Classification) classes:  | I.2.10; I.4.8\nL21: Cite as:  | cite12†arXiv:2601.10462 [cs.AI]\nL22:    | (or cite13†arXiv:2601.10462v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL23:    | cite14†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2601.10462†doi.or